<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_HuttCartel_Captives.xml   RimUtinni Patches · DROID_HUTT_CAPTIVES_1
                                 (packet C6), authored 2026-09-08
  ============================================================================

  Builds the purchase half of DROID_UNIFIED_FRAMEWORK_DESIGN.md §3.2's "Hutt
  captives" row: "droids in Hutt torture chambers — rescue or buy." §0 ruling 2,
  verbatim: "those trapped in the torture chambers of the Hutts for displeasing
  them."

  🔴 SCOPE, RECORDED HONESTLY: the "torture chambers" themselves are NOT a real,
  visitable site yet. `design/Jawa/templates/hutt_holding_pens.lua` is compiled
  and registered in GenStep_ComposeSettlementDistrict.TemplateFiles by label
  ("holding pens"), but that step's own doc comment says v1 "reads only
  districts[0]" per settlement, and Gorga the Immense's Palace's districts[0]
  is "palace hall" — "holding pens" is districts[2] and is never composed onto
  a real map today. Separately, no InhabitedCastDef exists for the Hutt Cartel
  at all (SettlementManifestDefs_GorgaPalace.xml's own header: "no
  InhabitedCastDef exists for any Cartel place yet"), and
  SettlementManifestDef.castSlots (the "guard"/"debtor" roles the manifest
  already names against "holding pens") is proven SCHEMA ONLY —
  WorldObject_Inhabited.InstantiateCast reads `Cast` (`castDef ??
  placeDef?.defaultCast`), never `manifest.castSlots` — so today Gorga's Palace
  spawns precisely ZERO cast pawns of any kind. Building multi-district
  composition and a real InhabitedCastDef for the Hutt Cartel is its own,
  much bigger prerequisite than a droid packet should absorb; it is not filed
  as a fresh item because DROID_FACTION_LOADOUTS_1's own C1 already recorded
  "Hutt captives in the torture chambers" as its own deferred line pointing at
  this item, and the site-composition gap belongs with whichever future item
  finishes DISTRICT_TEMPLATE_LIBRARY_1's own stated "stretch goal, unbuilt."

  What ships here instead, ready to plug into that site the moment it exists:
  the CONTENT. A dedicated TraderKindDef so a real, playable purchase route
  exists TODAY regardless of the map layer (caravan trading needs no map), plus
  RSW_DW_LiberateHuttCaptive (RecipeDefs_Droidworks.xml) for the rescue half.
  THE PLUG-IN POINT for whoever builds the site: give the "holding pens"
  district's "debtor" cast role an InhabitedCastDef whose roles use these same
  pawn kinds, routed through StockGenerator_DWHuttCaptives.ApplyCaptiveBolt (or
  an equivalent call to DroidworksBoltUtility.ApplyCaptiveBolt) at spawn time.

  Pawn kinds: non-combat, colonist-tier Droidworks kinds already MEASURED live
  in RUT_TradeMootDroids.xml's own stock (2026-09-08) — a debtor droid is a
  household/labour/protocol unit that displeased its master, not a war
  machine; Hutt's existing combat guards (RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkI/
  SentWD, JawaHuttCartel.xml pawnGroupMakers, C1) are untouched.

  Faction: `Jawa_HuttCartel` (this same mod's own FactionDef, JawaHuttCartel.xml,
  authored 2026-08-14) — the REAL, loadable Hutt Cartel FactionDef, not a
  stand-in. Recorded because DROIDWORKS_HEADS_BRAINS_SPIKES_1 (B3, same session)
  keyed its Hutt data-spike to `OuterRim_BinaryStarRaiders`, asserting "no
  dedicated Hutt Cartel FactionDef exists anywhere in the stack" — that
  assertion is WRONG as of this file: `Jawa_HuttCartel` is ours, is
  SettlementManifestDefs_GorgaPalace.xml's own `factionDefName`, and is exactly
  the Hutt faction this item's captives belong to. Not fixing B3's own
  already-closed item here (out of scope for C6); flagged so nobody re-derives
  the wrong convention from it.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <TraderKindDef MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">
    <defName>RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_Captives</defName>
    <label>Hutt debtor droids</label>
    <commonality>0.3</commonality>
    <requestable>true</requestable>
    <orbital>false</orbital>
    <stockGenerators>

      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>Silver</thingDef>
        <countRange>800~2000</countRange>
      </li>

      <!-- The captives themselves. resentmentSeverityRange left at the class
           default (0.2~0.8) — some are fresh, some are already past
           Recipe_RemoveRestrainingBolt.RebellionThreshold (0.6f): buying one
           is not always a clean purchase. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.StockGenerator_DWHuttCaptives">
        <countRange>1~3</countRange>
        <pawnKinds>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3LD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3PD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_T3UD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_OuterRim_ProtocolDroid</li>
        </pawnKinds>
      </li>

    </stockGenerators>
  </TraderKindDef>

</Defs>
